{"id": "clm:90dc542c7b26621cc0c812afa4d2940747f5efed4efff07250e2d10d131ab83b", "type": "statement", "text": "The German guideline publication in 2024 advises considering competing causes of cognitive impairment, including vitamin deficiencies and metabolic disorders, and reviewing medications with anticholinergic cognitive effects. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:ec576db7748a63a4189ec3c63764630c71893a08c0cea752c48febe4d5bbdd84"]}
{"id": "clm:df0c7402a0dc0aae9c4b6d66165f58e9f67778e6f71150dca30407fcde037889", "type": "statement", "text": "Memantine recommendations differ: NICE NG71 (2017) allows consideration only when cholinesterase inhibitors are contraindicated or not tolerated, whereas the 2024 German guideline recommends against memantine for PD dementia. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng71/chapter/recommendations", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:528e8a835d13533301a08e0fe6a81b5b6553f6920b5697c16b8418dbc3a27bb9", "ev:6afe6cee4c71ec1eb422f80cf9435f6638ca18a6a19449483923531d33f51808", "ev:e137b5eb4f66a8cbfee9ed089ebb0c051db874c6d361872ac8d3a750e647e17c"]}
{"id": "clm:c4350debb97a766c867fe97c5db32172a2eeb1f120600577bb864c6d00b76911", "type": "statement", "text": "The cited sources distinguish PD-MCI, where functional independence is preserved despite possible subtle difficulty with complex tasks, from Parkinson’s disease dementia, where cognitive impairment interferes with daily activities; motor disability alone does not establish dementia. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8073727/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:683dfeca5c61a8a4260997c171b5cfe97d6f25fffc75094ef04a51fedb2e136a", "ev:8e632bdad4c46e08a4d0213b07353033146d939076fa1b5558b88b85484f963c"]}
{"id": "clm:feab20a59abd3b94957ac8e774e2d276327ea7120821b74be325abadd4151e0a", "type": "statement", "text": "NICE NG71 (2017) recommends offering a cholinesterase inhibitor for mild or moderate Parkinson’s disease dementia and considering one for severe dementia; the severe-dementia recommendation has weaker wording. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)", "source_url": "https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng71/chapter/recommendations", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2a5cb1b7fe54263d6e2115f3a060cbd4b391443cad8ed900d29d1eae61f0f336", "ev:5fdb27de1cda6461564637227b61dfc1cb02a7bd935b7146b72910583a7bdf69"]}
{"id": "clm:55fb0fc639b82b6f5fd06769b20553523bb471cc49c3b4e0ea6520c7cacbd217", "type": "statement", "text": "In the 2004 placebo-controlled PD dementia trial, 541 patients were enrolled; rivastigmine was studied for 24 weeks and produced moderate benefits. ADAS-cog improved by 2.1 points with rivastigmine versus worsening by 0.7 points with placebo. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15590953/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:80b8ced5807a82cb1fc7e6f747df5c8bb158b7a11eb46324b115452ba5f9f4aa", "ev:934c96f43d9ff605d17d1247fb4d5c5e9c507a5592095bdb05bb6b404290ccbb", "ev:ee5511f7a5f3c29afec473fcf6d4e314687cb46bf9f00095cad895a131c91e90"]}
{"id": "clm:783b311e3c594a681443987f86da78a86d82973e14d74be6a58bd9df9ef77d9d", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2004 PD dementia trial reported nausea in 29.0 percent versus 11.2 percent, vomiting in 16.6 percent versus 1.7 percent, and tremor in 10.2 percent versus 3.9 percent with rivastigmine versus placebo, respectively. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15590953/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1da4ba59c1e7a13823e80c37b6cf3da40d4c63677e7961bd2b0a2c3e4d5d0436", "ev:934c96f43d9ff605d17d1247fb4d5c5e9c507a5592095bdb05bb6b404290ccbb"]}
{"id": "clm:b82211bcc291368bece96524e8bcce5d019fda94beec1d718d0c6879405584b9", "type": "statement", "text": "The cited sources describe assessing cognitive complaints using patient and care-partner history plus cognitive testing; a brief global screen such as MoCA can support an abbreviated assessment, while comprehensive neuropsychological assessment evaluates individual domains rather than relying only on one global score. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8073727/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a36cf6f8cda30a441d197c069b7c0213c224cf159dfd376be7f847c69b5225f9", "ev:e22227107bdcdf97a0a86c7b1b0af837c8aa0fc6b4d73c267d743f790bd2479d"]}
{"id": "clm:8812d9bc85feca9501723a280498d6c42c7d86a85eabb6eeacebea854bbee1bd", "type": "statement", "text": "Rivastigmine offers modest symptomatic cognitive benefit in Parkinson’s disease dementia. In the 24-week placebo-controlled trial, mean ADAS-cog improved by 2.1 points with rivastigmine versus a 0.7-point worsening with placebo; this trial result does not establish prevention of dementia progression. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15590953/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2445ad31c9b6340f38bd6473907f0970e19cdf269aa3497f9a6a4e79f595887d", "ev:9a194a383a156965b783b06654d46c76844d5faf145a4b6a1171db85af78bf3f", "ev:ee5511f7a5f3c29afec473fcf6d4e314687cb46bf9f00095cad895a131c91e90"]}
{"id": "clm:0805477afe291bcc7a3aabbf16bc1498cc01652439093f7d7d93ea03d969411f", "type": "statement", "text": "Cognitive training has mixed evidence: the German guideline supports it for PD-MCI but notes small, heterogeneous trials; an eight-week computerized-training RCT in PD patients with subjective cognitive complaints found no benefit on primary planning accuracy and no group differences at follow-up. The populations and interventions differ, so this is a limitation on generalization rather than proof that every training program fails. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35248830/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:37885324d3b55de1f42b8667907a075a178cac3591736ff7fde87eb153639c45", "ev:9d177463a0f88cb8ccd58940bc28e2ff65ab2497e24ff2e87a1fa0fbd7778deb", "ev:aacfea4cbbfc6e054b2b4bbedc0a48ff3ab6b387b34961eee85fb31f184b347e"]}
{"id": "clm:caf5984041f46ccbf669fb8bf739e180e81201c3d1c5dbf52a014b82e5667ac6", "type": "statement", "text": "Assessment combines patient and informant history with cognitive testing. MDS Level I is abbreviated; Level II uses comprehensive testing across five cognitive domains, with two tests per domain. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8073727/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6a9a003b3b1ca4f91e73271673ca07c5b89f5170e9f3b1f8575618b25ac19baf", "ev:ac7aa24ebce063472fd051135bfd8c41d6d64e1294de07fa6642624b7eb7f98e", "ev:e30a3dc06fc832960719881f9e8742e002b4c6b5e0d87bcbe52ba6c01c857c6b"]}
{"id": "clm:ad2773198c302048c2128bc2098594cea296bc9c29e48fa8bd00afbfcde05930", "type": "statement", "text": "Rivastigmine has the strongest established drug evidence for PD dementia: the 2019 MDS review rates it efficacious and clinically useful, and the 2024 German guideline recommends its use. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2445ad31c9b6340f38bd6473907f0970e19cdf269aa3497f9a6a4e79f595887d", "ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:3f93107b2208d5c1b73b683cb866089dca482fb49dc16dd739f86f10b69faa33", "ev:6ba983933805b0db375bf94a1366385cd41cac2f44b73a02f75acd9ed5792680", "ev:9a4f9a666b79d0cc757054dd32212b7602e4760d1043d61417321b7b385ff5a3", "ev:e2983a6508a69ec949ac6cc5492f1845b3d72da9e7f74620ca8cf72f9a5d0268"]}
{"id": "clm:5e345a6b920159f27f662fc9aab16014459ad41a8f4a7ee1b42d8a92a287091b", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2019 MDS review classifies rivastigmine for nondementia cognitive impairment as investigational with insufficient evidence; the 2024 German guideline recommends against rivastigmine, donepezil, galantamine and memantine for PD-MCI. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:3f93107b2208d5c1b73b683cb866089dca482fb49dc16dd739f86f10b69faa33", "ev:8213d5adff4c0c30c3493ee6139002bec3106e975719576605efb3b95374485d", "ev:beecd5206d5418112ed6ca0247ebacd86521b2c25c83afa9f704ae5a894d63cc", "ev:eb4013d792a148452faf4cbb0dd84afc3c4a4a2ac1489787d36cad1fed1ce2fa"]}
{"id": "clm:f1ef336bd13ba17acf969f86a7d1f87c623e09fd91cc1f38bf2fc6b6e4298a61", "type": "statement", "text": "A 28-participant PD-MCI rivastigmine patch crossover trial found a nonsignificant trend on its global primary outcome and no treatment effect on cognitive measures; a positive secondary everyday-cognition measure does not establish broad cognitive efficacy. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25914281/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:389c4ea85b0407e14539aaae7fcd0b054364ff06d4623b867f02fe754656997f", "ev:6f0e49b879546bb1e02f8a6a24b787c0d6235740ed7936e7c6106fa3584429ad", "ev:d0d4ddd15bab9a6e8569586119f9ff24f4417011630129f3d8dac68a12819ab6"]}
{"id": "clm:5c196b76826fb7b72537050c58486393f03de953354d45b9450b81362371e983", "type": "statement", "text": "Donepezil has weaker evidence than rivastigmine in PD dementia: MDS in 2019 retained insufficient efficacy evidence but rated it possibly useful, while the 2024 German guideline permits possible off-label use. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:2d0cd5421e6b7884f380466fe937ca440ba74ac57a965794f87c269184402eb8", "ev:3f93107b2208d5c1b73b683cb866089dca482fb49dc16dd739f86f10b69faa33", "ev:4fd032658c7a3cedc15aafd24eb5dfd47725b1b7696ee04fdaa871968cfbda96", "ev:d7d9f30e629a09caa421ee15177492e508338a1e55836e03983fe8f855a6a999"]}
{"id": "clm:560e175be9edac371333c1c8027623083984d0a7625423df011eb37c28930899", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2024 German guideline says cognitive training can be offered for PD-MCI and cognitive stimulation can be offered for PD dementia; these are distinct interventions tailored to different levels of cognitive impairment. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:4980bce2339a33654d685595ac56e5a8f4c685538338755f9275ccb60198a41d", "ev:9a7dda460f89c9bc6880c0606cb9cd7446a6fc6a918ef95bc563d5bb39b6bb98", "ev:d68d9a0837755915ee9de63dea61b2b6d46da091d25a90aec42a8402e3db8fca", "ev:e1b14672899718cbc027af4e8d918654fe7dc461cbcd119cbc17cf4c8b52055c", "ev:e1e82164478152f16ef576c4a7b5b6d0f6c60ccc3fa3c6d499aca9d093f0d515"]}
{"id": "clm:69e7c641e37992bd9398d74245d04a46c4a49aef07b6c68a2d96feabce5ac49f", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2024 German guideline recommends aerobic training for PD-MCI, while explaining that the suggested schedule is based on expert consensus and the optimal intensity and frequency have not been established. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:4352e917ee05198d9c7b1a4ec71d4d2764145bb21009c250658ff90c2dc5ae1a", "ev:49110fc29428579005f93140bd95246eb15006ea078b01e43431feb0514eb68f"]}
{"id": "clm:cea630bdab4351e7bfa258a330ef863aad57b0e721b972a423274caaa4a57ebb", "type": "statement", "text": "Cognitive training should not be presented as proven durable prevention: a PD-MCI trial reported memory benefit at six months but not twelve, while a separate broader PD trial found no cognitive advantage or difference in conversion of cognitive status at one or two years. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8563628/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10724826/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5a3e962d53f4a838fbd078327bdf04136bc2860ac6e11e6e644845bd0ac0c71e", "ev:a1264cb315091ca721134434c411bf84a4ae9fd39b6aa0fba94f17e0e6eb1696"]}
{"id": "clm:e6e1f4d8d76fa027ba62f5bf7ecbccb013bf298e682895ec3d27396f36293cb7", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2024 German guideline advises against using food supplements or herbal therapeutics to treat cognitive deficits in PD-MCI or PD dementia. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:43a0b6d07fa701d759c5bec6db4d02c2c443acb26034602a8867979089ffe299", "ev:48383cd7d05ad04a226ebd939ab6285990c5cb41a7460618579e8fdc66ad270f"]}
{"id": "clm:3c7073e37453e145746817f2bebb8914b7a630bcebb2716fbb76113850033183", "type": "statement", "text": "Galantamine recommendations also differ by guideline and date: the 2019 MDS review calls it possibly useful despite insufficient PD dementia efficacy evidence; the 2024 German guideline recommends against its use. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6916382/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:14f48f5aa9bb1c8c63396f2639a0ab91bdaf0f9a19c520d6f24f7a4c513ee666", "ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:3f93107b2208d5c1b73b683cb866089dca482fb49dc16dd739f86f10b69faa33", "ev:f784d06d079352c7d3a34a61f90b1eaca0cfa706856d49a52924ff29dd29c2bc"]}
{"id": "clm:015dff8fb01e88b1a963fe98615b38d1ca074ff344dd4a88aac553972e251892", "type": "statement", "text": "A 2021 clinical review recommends evaluating reversible contributors before attributing all cognitive change to PD, including anticholinergic drugs, benzodiazepines, opioids, and metabolic or nutritional contributors assessed through appropriate laboratory testing. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8073727/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0d77101004189655386fd83c6afe6f3375cafe5d3301acf658c929afc27cb6f3", "ev:3b5613bc0ce50c96b6c2b7c3b49b4087099987f2bc1de5091d62f70cc0c8bba4"]}
{"id": "clm:6f4130d46f765962e6a2d1ed1402701e03e88136aa052a6eeb075822f29827b8", "type": "statement", "text": "Rivastigmine’s cognitive benefit must be balanced against tolerability: its dementia trial found more nausea, vomiting and tremor than placebo, and the German guideline also recognizes tremor and worsening PD symptoms as adverse effects. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15590953/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:103b47ec35fb24d33e42a8c8d3824ba6b572c9ecc4c200c31f33d2c0803dd625", "ev:1da4ba59c1e7a13823e80c37b6cf3da40d4c63677e7961bd2b0a2c3e4d5d0436", "ev:ee5511f7a5f3c29afec473fcf6d4e314687cb46bf9f00095cad895a131c91e90"]}
{"id": "clm:10919b1c620b32e423c86b448c59c0c524cdf0f3cd76a1f3d55258f9103832f7", "type": "statement", "text": "Dementia drug evidence should not be extrapolated to PD-MCI. The 2024 German guideline recommends against rivastigmine, donepezil, galantamine and memantine for PD-MCI; the 2021 review likewise found no effective pharmacologic treatment for PD-MCI. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8073727/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0d77101004189655386fd83c6afe6f3375cafe5d3301acf658c929afc27cb6f3", "ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:9093cd88de885f89f996f54d847d09f96e81f78b2b490bab525c214021e33272", "ev:f4f12ca86de4479ca3041dc87809fdd457618c29675476eaf99388dc2616687d"]}
{"id": "clm:f3d8175fd51205b737c3a6e90eb6d7bf921772652a55fc00f8ed278df8b85cf1", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2024 German guideline recommends rivastigmine for PDD and says donepezil might be used off label; it does not regard all cholinesterase inhibitors as equally supported. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2ba8a8a117602d8157b4d9475fe83281d6c784250fc2305e49105793c1aabf92", "ev:aac4944f672eb22aee21ad5820a8fb292d770581e5603ccbc101433d70df12d8"]}
{"id": "clm:6a8519d6da3444ed0561e58703817ec3fa16d2b09b0000e493f1ad6a3247f823", "type": "statement", "text": "For PDD, the German guideline says cognitive stimulation can be offered and reminiscence therapy might be offered; it distinguishes these approaches from targeted cognitive training for PD-MCI. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11561078/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:144d0904c60b8c529562bce4f2cab1aa7333cf68bca953698d1c4357b2a12ee6", "ev:e1b14672899718cbc027af4e8d918654fe7dc461cbcd119cbc17cf4c8b52055c"]}
